  "headline": "Government Clarifies Plans For School Construction At UI Site",
  "seoTitle": "Government Clarifies School Plans At UI",
  "metaDescription": "Government officials have clarified that a planned school project will not be located within the forest area of the University of Indonesia campus.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Minister of Social Affairs Saifullah Yusuf confirmed that the proposed school project will not occupy the University of Indonesia forest.",
    "Earlier reports regarding the use of the urban forest area for the development have been formally addressed by government representatives.",
    "The project remains in the early stages of assessment, with officials now considering alternative locations for the school site."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government is evaluating potential sites for a new public school initiative, initially sparking concerns regarding the use of land belonging to the University of Indonesia. Following public discussion, Minister of Social Affairs Saifullah Yusuf and other government officials have explicitly stated that the project will not be situated within the University of Indonesia's urban forest. While preliminary discussions had involved land in the vicinity, officials clarified that the protected forest zone is excluded from development plans. The initiative is currently undergoing a comprehensive review process, and authorities are now exploring alternative locations for the proposed facility. This clarification serves to address reports that had previously linked the school project to the university's forested campus area, while emphasizing that the planning phase is still ongoing and requires further feasibility studies before a final site is selected.",
